From 8ae589ac5719e647ecc6c4da887268f64b8bcb46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:02:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: only drink cure potions for food when actually hurt

When the borg is weak from hunger and has no food, borg_eat_food_any()
falls back to cure potions, which nourish a little.  The guard is meant
to allow this only "when hurting", but it tested CURHP <= MAXHP, which
is always true, so the borg drank Cure Light/Serious/Critical Wounds or
Healing potions at full hit points.  The caller tries this before the
Remove Hunger and Herbal Curing spells, so a Druid or Ranger that could
cast Remove Hunger drank a Potion of Healing instead, for one percent of
nourishment.

Test CURHP < MAXHP so the potions are used for food only when they also
heal.  At full hit points the caller goes on to the hunger spells, or to
leaving the level for food.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#80.
---
 src/borg/borg-item-use.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-item-use.c b/src/borg/borg-item-use.c
index 020b03bbb..35dd08db6 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-item-use.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-item-use.c
@@ -394,7 +394,7 @@ bool borg_eat_food_any(void)
     }
     /* Consume in order, when hurting */
     if ((borg.trait[BI_CURHP] < 4
-            || (borg.trait[BI_CURHP] <= borg.trait[BI_MAXHP]))
+            || (borg.trait[BI_CURHP] < borg.trait[BI_MAXHP]))
         && (borg_quaff_potion(sv_potion_cure_light)
             || borg_quaff_potion(sv_potion_cure_serious)
             || borg_quaff_potion(sv_potion_cure_critical)
